eggs/
.eggs/
# Anchored to the repo root. Unanchored, `lib/` matched `web/lib/` too and
# swallowed api.ts, domSelection.ts and selectionSet.ts -- the API client and
# the client-side region geometry. They had never been committed, so a fresh
# clone could not build the frontend. The rule comes from a Python packaging
# template where it means build output at the top level, which is what it now
# says.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# PyInstaller
